    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0500" n="1234" xml:id="pg1234"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mavroyeni Bey to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In an interview which I
                    had with your excellency’s worthy predecessor on the 4th of April last, the late
                    Mr. Gresham expressed some uneasiness with regard to the American Female College
                    at Scutari, and requested me to write to Constantinople for information on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>The Sublime Porte has just informed me, in reply to my inquiry, that not only has
                    that college never been closed, but that it has been the recipient of an
                    altogether special favor in being exempted from the moukata’a, to which all
                    educational institutions in the Empire are subject.</p>
                <p>This exemption, which is without precedent, has been granted by His Imperial
                    Majesty the Sultan as an evidence of his sincere desire that the relations of
                    friendship which so happily exist between the two States may be maintained on a
                    footing of the greatest cordiality.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mavroyeni.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
